  "schema_version": 1,
  "jsp": "JSP-000397",
  "erdos": 491,
  "title": "If an additive arithmetic function has uniformly bounded differences at consecutive integers, must it be close to a logarithmic function?",
  "scope": "For a real-valued arithmetic function additive on coprime arguments, uniformly bounded consecutive differences imply f(n)=c log(n)+O(1) as n tends to infinity. More quantitatively, a nonnegative bound M on the absolute consecutive differences gives a coefficient c with |f(n)-c log(n)| <= 2M for every positive integer n; complete additivity of the original function is not assumed and exact equality with c log(n) is not asserted.",
  "attribution": "Existing plby formalization of the affirmative result attributed to Wirsing (Wi70), with Erdos (Er46) as related prior work. Original source bytes and headers are preserved; no new-proof or first-formalization claim.",
  "target_module": "ErdosProblems.Erdos491",
